  "result": "The gate passes: it returned **OK — 13 witnesses, 21 names, composes nothing** on the second of six allowed runs. My first run was on the unedited skeleton to get a baseline, and it returned the expected UNUSED_CLAIM.\n\n**The rule** (`NRS_484B_413_3.lean`):\n- **Who it binds:** the subject must be a member of DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle.\n- **When it applies:** both of these at the same observation:\n  - Either the subject has just come to a complete halt that is not excused, or it has just started decelerating at or beyond `p.sudden_decel_min`.\n  - Another vehicle is behind it in the same lane, within `p.rear_signal_reach`.\n- **Excused halts** follow DEF-NRS-484A-260:\n  - a road user ahead in the same lane within `p.queue_halt_gap`;\n  - or the subject is in a travel region governed by any of these:\n    - a stop sign or a yield sign;\n    - a traffic signal showing circular red, flashing red, or a red arrow;\n    - a railway signal with lights flashing, or its gate lowering or down;\n    - a police officer directing stop.\n- **What it requires:** brake lamps lit or a stop-or-slow arm signal, at the halt or deceleration or at some point in the `p.stop_signal_lead_window` before it.\n- **Red arrow:** the node gave no direction, so I wrote all four directions.\n- **Narrowings:** none. Every span is written as the node maps it.\n\n**The witnesses** (`NRS_484B_413_3.lean` in the witness folder): the six planned scenarios, plus seven extra branches so that every excuse and the arm signal is tested by at least one scenario:\n- one each for the yield sign, the red signal, the flashing railway lights, the lowered railway gate, and the police officer;\n- one for a queued car 2 m ahead;\n- one where the arm signal alone makes the halt compliant.\n\nAll of them use one lane and 16 frames at 0.5 s, with the halt or deceleration at 4.0 s. The gate only judges 4.0–7.5 s, so the full 3 s look-back fits inside the trace and the first frame, which has nothing before it, is never judged.\n\n`task_result.md` in the working directory has the full record.",
